A||||4||batboy||unusual tire wear||||1||
Z||000000||batboy||03-09-2000||03:52 PM||||My 85 GT pulls a little to the left. The previous owner told me it did that ever since it was new. I've checked tire air pressure numerous times, I've rotated tires, and I've even switched tires. I've replaced all the tie rod ends, front wheel bearings, and the steering stabilizer. Ball joints, brakes, control arm bushings, and steering rack have been triple checked. I've had a four wheel alignment done. I finally discovered that one of the upper shock mount brackets was loose, so I repaired that. Still it pulls to the left.<P>The driver's side rear tire always is the one with the unusual wear. There is cupping evident, mainly on the outer part of the tread, and it is wearing badly in the middle of the tread. Middle tread wear aften happens if you're running the tire over-inflated, but this is not the case. That leaves either a bad alignment or a bad strut, but the struts and shocks seems ok. I have a print-out of the alignment numbers and everything looks to be in specs. Is the alignment shop ripping me off (work done on my other vehicles in the past was ok) or is there a bad strut and I just don't realize it. Is there anything I'm missing? This is driving me crazy.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||03-09-2000||04:45 PM||||Could be a shot rear wheel bearing. I believe that these are not replaceable you need a new unit.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||03-09-2000||04:52 PM||||Make sure they are doing a full blown 4 wheel alignment. Not just the front-only or a thrust alignment. Does the print out show camber and toe numbers for the rear?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||03-09-2000||10:30 PM||||The rear wheel bearings appear to have no play and they roll smoothly. I paid for a 4 wheel alignment and yes there were specs listed for the rear.<P>Ok, it took awhile, but I finally found my printout. I noticed an odd thing this time that I didn't see before. The before and after camber settings (front and rear) are the same and are still out of specs in the after column. Them lazy bastards! Both rear corners are very close, but the front left and right are about one degree out of the range. The left front caster is a 1/2 degree out of spec. I think I'm going to have a nice long chat with those people. They're either doing it again for free with me looking their shoulders or they're giving me my money back. Could this be affecting my left rear tire wear? I know it could account for the way it pulls to one side on the highway. This pisses me off!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bruce||03-10-2000||12:36 AM||||Is the body frame ok?||||reg||1
